; `break` gives up the innermost open thing (todo 31, 2026-10-14): in the `proof` of a `show`, only
; the `proof` -- the claim stays open for a new `proof`; right after the `show`, or after that
; `break`, a `break` withdraws the claim. Before, the first `break` discarded the claim too. A
; withdrawn claim is a `todo` (2026-10-15: the grader counted a file of withdrawn claims as complete).
load propositional
prop A, B
use A

show A and A
proof
    break
proof                         ; a new attempt at the same claim (before: "no claim to prove")
    A and A
qed

show B                        ; withdrawn at once: nothing open, nothing added -- a `todo`
break
expect "ProofError"
    B

show B
proof
    break
break                         ; the proof, then the claim
expect "ProofError"
    B

expect "ProofError" "has no proof"
    load "helpers/break-leaves-the-claim-open.kurt"
